  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> attached to a spring is made to oscillate with an initial amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> minutes the amplitude decreases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Determine the value of the damping constant for this motion. (take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></math>&nbsp;)"
  },
